<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">French Somaliland</h1><p class="st-meta">1896 CE – 1967 CE · capital Djibouti</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">France's colony on the Gulf of Aden around the port of Djibouti, the sea outlet of Ethiopia through its famous railway.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1896 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> combined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/obock">Obock</a> and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a> over the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-tadjoura">Sultanate of Tadjoura</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issa-clan">Issa Somali</a> coast into the colony of the Cote francaise des <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somalis</a>, with its capital at the new port of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/djibouti">Djibouti</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonce-lagarde">Leonce Lagarde</a>. The borders were fixed by agreements with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The colony lived on its port and on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/djibouti">Djibouti</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a> railway, completed in 1917, which carried most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia's</a> foreign trade. Its population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issa-clan">Issa Somali</a> pastoralists, Arab traders and French officials was small. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it sided with Vichy until British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> forced it to join <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-france">Free France</a> in 1942.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In referendums in 1958 and 1967 voters chose to remain French, amid protests and charges of manipulation. In 1967 the colony was renamed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-territory-of-the-afars-and-the-issas">French Territory of the Afars and the Issas</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-somaliland.jpg" alt="French Somaliland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1896 CE – 1967 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Djibouti</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Leonce Lagarde</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French, Afar, Somali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/djibouti">Djibouti</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cote francaise des Somalis, French Coast of the Somalis</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=french-somaliland" aria-label="French Somaliland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5867 1745 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where French Somaliland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6187 2001L6179 1994M6187 2001L6190 1987M6187 2001L5054 728M6187 2001L6187 2001"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6179 1994h0M6190 1987h0M5054 728h0M6187 2001h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6187 2001h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6187 2001h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Djibouti. <a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=french-somaliland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
